From: Codex Executor <codex-executor@local>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 01:58:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 20/23] sheet route: root-cause the carrier feature size and
 the volume mesher instead of gating

Two things were being papered over: a gate that refused cells whose cut nearly contains a cell edge or corner, and an
HXT retry when Gmsh produced a nonmanifold volume mesh. Both are removed; the causes are fixed upstream.

The residual sliver families are harmless. Sweeping the gap from 0.2 h to 0.002 h with the gate disabled: the strip
family passes every guard at every gap and the operator converges smoothly (energy steps 5.1e-3 down to 1.7e-4, the
geometry itself changing by the gap); the corner family gives the identical operator at every gap because the corner
region is void and its slivers are zero rows. The gate becomes a receipt diagnostic.

The Gmsh failure was a feature-size problem, not a sliver problem: the frozen carrier with aspect-1e3 slivers meshes
cleanly, while a merge radius of 1/10 h left 0.003 carrier edges next to 0.03 sheet triangles and the cap, a
constrained triangulation of the carrier, was refined to that size. The merge radius is now set by the surface scale
(1/3 h = 0.0104, at least half the remesh size), so no carrier edge is below it: the failing cell goes from 31
nonmanifold facets to 0, and the carrier improves as well (maximum aspect ratio median 7.0 to 2.7 on the c=0
population, 8.0 to 3.1 on tilted planes).

The cap PSLG carried features of 1e-4 and below. A feature-size invariant (0.2 remesh) moves a chain vertex onto a
nearby carrier node or edge and snaps a crossing to a nearby chain vertex. Keeping the sheet a manifold needed five
rules, each found by a failure: carrier nodes never move; ring nodes on another clip plane are never targets and
vertices on another plane never move; one chain vertex per target and none chain-adjacent to an assigned vertex; a
fold check on the incident sheet triangles; and crossings are never snapped onto a carrier node.

After both, legacy Delaunay still overlapped tetrahedra on an ordinary quality-0.15 cap triangle and segfaulted on 2
of 60 cells, while HXT meshed every one at equal quality. HXT is now the algorithm of record with the generation
thread count pinned to 1 (it is byte-identical at a fixed count and differs between counts); the crash retry is gone
and a nonmanifold mesh fails closed.

Results: the six cells that ever failed all PASS with 0 nonmanifold facets and 0 non-manifold surface edges; 60-cell
run 58 PASS + 2 EMPTY, 0 failures; 2x1x1 cut block assembled vs constrained monolithic -4.5e-5 to 4.5e-3 (was 1.4e-4
to 6.4e-3), interface mismatch 0; 21 tests pass. STEP6 report section 7 records the analysis.

